{"analysis":"Version 0 scored best (69.8) by labelling a tweet positive or negative when a stance was plain, even if mild. Version 1 demanded strong feeling and pushed 82 positive and 69 negative texts into neutral (66.2). Version 2 counted any lean and pushed 69 neutral texts into positive and 49 into negative (65.0). The right line is between them, close to version 0. Neutral texts version 2 got wrong but version 1 got right:
- personal plans and logistics: going to a concert, getting in line, picking something up;
- ticket sales, 'anyone wanna buy', 'who wants to go', 'are you going?';
- event listings with prices and times;
- sports commentary and critique of players;
- debating replies;
- mild 'still waiting' remarks.
Positive and negative texts version 1 got wrong but versions 0 and 2 got right:
- openly emotive promos ('come see me!!');
- expressions of wanting or looking forward ('I want IHOP');
- RIP and condolences;
- small personal miseries marked by :(, #fml or #boring.
Version 3 uses version 0 as the base and adds these distinctions. Plans, tickets, listings and invitations stay neutral unless the author shows their own excitement or love. Emoticon or hashtag misery is negative. Commentary on athletes and debating replies stay neutral unless the tone is hostile.","question":"What overall sentiment does the tweet's author express, judging by a clear attitude, mood or evaluation rather than the topic alone?","rule":"Use positive or negative when the author's own feeling is plain, even mildly (love, want, can't wait, RIP; :(, #fml, boring, sucks). Plans, logistics, ticket sales, event listings, 'who wants to go?' and 'are you going?' are neutral unless the author shows personal excitement. Sports commentary, critiques of players, debating replies, mild 'still waiting' remarks and plain news are neutral unless openly hostile, mocking or emotional.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Author shows enthusiasm, love, praise, eager wanting, gratitude, condolences or excited self-promotion.","examples":["It’s Tuesday night in Athens! AKA karaoke night at the Volstead so come see me!!","noel fielding may be one of the greatest people alive.","I want IHOP tomorrow morning","I just heard about Frank Gifford. Anyone who ever watched Monday Night Football enjoyed it more with him. Rest in peace."],"cues":"can't wait, so excited, love, best, greatest, looking forward, I want, rest in peace, <3, yasssss","not_for":"Plain plans, ticket sales, listings and 'who's coming?' questions are neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"News, facts, questions, plans, logistics, ticket sales, event listings, sports commentary, debating replies, offhand remarks without clear feeling.","examples":["Ed Sheeran concert at 7 PM tomorrow. Getting in line at like 9 lol. Need to get close to the stage bruh","One spare Runrig ticket for next Friday night at the barrowlands! Pm me for details @user","Imma need Brook Lopez to get more aggressive on the boards. 7 feet tall, c’mon son","its the 63rd of july and we are still waiting for frank ocean's new album"],"cues":"tomorrow, tickets, pm me, who wants to, are you going, still waiting, may, should, score","not_for":"Open gushing is positive; insults, ridicule, sadness or :( are negative."},"negative":{"what":"Author complains, is disappointed, sad, bored or annoyed, insults, mocks, or uses sarcasm.","examples":["Dream High 2 sucks compared to the 1st one.","Just remembered I'm taking the PSSAs tomorrow. #Fml","A Thursday night with no Waterloo road on! #boring","The best way to find Malaysia Airlines Flight MH370 may be with Michelle Obama's arms."],"cues":"sucks, disappointed, #fml, #boring, :(, hate, can't go, wtf, #sarcasm","not_for":"Swearing for excitement is positive; plain critique of athletes or mild waiting is neutral."}}}

{"analysis":"Version 5 scored 71.7, slightly below version 4's 72.5. Several neutral rules in version 5 pulled positive recall down from 158 to 144: plain game results, asking a friend along, and team or injury news. The gain on neutral-to-positive errors (45 to 34) did not make up for this. Negative recall rose from 156 to 166, helped by the can't-make-it and sarcasm cues, but more neutral texts were again labelled negative (29 to 41). Most of these are wry or joking self-remarks and pointed opinions on public figures. Version 5 had dropped version 4's distress qualifier on opinions and its teasing-celebrities clause, and moved wry self-jokes from the main criteria into the negative not_for.

The gold labels are noisy around these boundaries, so wholesale shifts mostly trade one error for another. Version 6 goes back to version 4 and keeps only the narrow gains from version 5:
- can't-make-it and 'but I can't' cues for negative;
- a short note, only in the positive not_for, that plain score updates are neutral. This should cut the most obvious game-report false positives without the broader neutral rules.
The 'come enjoy, join us' wording for public promos stays positive. Asking a single friend along gets no special rule. Opinion, teasing and wry self-joke texts stay neutral without insults or clear distress, as in version 4.","question":"What overall sentiment does the tweet's author express, judging by a clear attitude, mood or evaluation rather than the topic alone?","rule":"Use positive or negative when the author's own feeling is plain, even if mild. Invitations to come enjoy or join an event, giveaways, and reports of achievements, milestones or wins of note are positive. Plain ticket sales, listings, logistics and 'are you going?' are neutral. Wry jokes about one's own situation, teasing of celebrities, corrections, and opinions or arguments about politics, religion or sport without insults or clear distress are neutral. Personal setbacks (can't make it, can't go) and news of violence or scandal are negative.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Enthusiasm, love, praise, eager wanting, condolences, inviting promos, giveaways, or reported achievements and milestones.","examples":["Come enjoy Splash Dance with Robbie Riviera this Thursday @user","8th strikeout of the afternoon for David Price's 100th career win!","noel fielding may be one of the greatest people alive.","I want IHOP tomorrow morning"],"cues":"come enjoy, join us, invite your friends, chance to win, can't wait, love, best, rest in peace, <3","not_for":"Ticket sales, price listings, plain plans and plain score updates are neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Facts, questions, listings, ticket sales, logistics, sports commentary, debating replies, corrections, wry or joking remarks without real complaint.","examples":["One spare Runrig ticket for next Friday night at the barrowlands! Pm me for details @user","Wantin to go out tonite....but no one to go out with so i guess i'll be on netflix  tonite","@user You do realize that the 1st Amendment doesn't just apply to Christians, right?","Imma need Brook Lopez to get more aggressive on the boards. 7 feet tall, c’mon son"],"cues":"pm me, tickets, are you going, I guess, still waiting, right?, may, should, heads up","not_for":"Open gushing is positive; insults, sadness, :(, #fml or can't-make-it regrets are negative."},"negative":{"what":"Clear complaint, disappointment, sadness, boredom, personal setback, insult, mockery or sarcasm, or news of a clearly bad event.","examples":["Dream High 2 sucks compared to the 1st one.","Just remembered I'm taking the PSSAs tomorrow. #Fml","I wanna go to the studio with Ulysses n them tomorrow,but i cant. #BARS","The best way to find Malaysia Airlines Flight MH370 may be with Michelle Obama's arms."],"cues":"sucks, disappointed, #fml, #boring, :(, but I can't, hate, injured, shot dead, wtf","not_for":"Wry self-jokes, mild critique of athletes and argumentative replies are neutral."}}}

{"analysis":"Version 6 is the best so far (73.5), so version 7 makes only small, targeted changes. The remaining errors are mostly noise at the boundaries. Similar texts carry opposite gold labels, for example 'A Thursday night with no Waterloo road on! #boring' (negative) and 'Wth am i supposed to do with my Thursday night with no Grey's nor Scandal?!' (neutral). Big rule shifts have traded one error type for another.

One group of neutral-to-positive errors is consistent: appeals for votes, retweets or support, and casual 'who wants to go with me?' or 'how about you & I go see' messages to friends. Examples are 'keep voting!!', 'Please RETWEET', 'OMG. Who wants to go see Duelo with me this Friday!?' and 'how about you & I go see Janet Jackson'. Annotators labelled all of these neutral. Version 5 added a broad rule for asking friends and also changed other things, which lost positive recall. So this time I add these cues only to the neutral cues and the positive not_for, without touching the public 'come enjoy, join us' promo wording.

Everything else stays as in version 6.","question":"What overall sentiment does the tweet's author express, judging by a clear attitude, mood or evaluation rather than the topic alone?","rule":"Use positive or negative when the author's own feeling is plain, even if mild. Invitations to come enjoy or join an event, giveaways, and reports of achievements, milestones or wins of note are positive. Plain ticket sales, listings, logistics, voting or retweet appeals, and 'are you going?' are neutral. Wry jokes about one's own situation, teasing of celebrities, corrections, and opinions or arguments about politics, religion or sport without insults or clear distress are neutral. Personal setbacks (can't make it, can't go) and news of violence or scandal are negative.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Enthusiasm, love, praise, eager wanting, condolences, inviting promos, giveaways, or reported achievements and milestones.","examples":["Come enjoy Splash Dance with Robbie Riviera this Thursday @user","8th strikeout of the afternoon for David Price's 100th career win!","noel fielding may be one of the greatest people alive.","I want IHOP tomorrow morning"],"cues":"come enjoy, join us, invite your friends, chance to win, can't wait, love, best, rest in peace, <3","not_for":"Ticket sales, price listings, plain plans, plain score updates, 'keep voting' and 'who wants to go with me?' are neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Facts, questions, listings, ticket sales, logistics, sports commentary, debating replies, corrections, wry or joking remarks without real complaint.","examples":["One spare Runrig ticket for next Friday night at the barrowlands! Pm me for details @user","Wantin to go out tonite....but no one to go out with so i guess i'll be on netflix  tonite","@user You do realize that the 1st Amendment doesn't just apply to Christians, right?","Imma need Brook Lopez to get more aggressive on the boards. 7 feet tall, c’mon son"],"cues":"pm me, tickets, are you going, who wants to go with me, keep voting, please retweet, I guess, still waiting, right?, may, should","not_for":"Open gushing is positive; insults, sadness, :(, #fml or can't-make-it regrets are negative."},"negative":{"what":"Clear complaint, disappointment, sadness, boredom, personal setback, insult, mockery or sarcasm, or news of a clearly bad event.","examples":["Dream High 2 sucks compared to the 1st one.","Just remembered I'm taking the PSSAs tomorrow. #Fml","I wanna go to the studio with Ulysses n them tomorrow,but i cant. #BARS","The best way to find Malaysia Airlines Flight MH370 may be with Michelle Obama's arms."],"cues":"sucks, disappointed, #fml, #boring, :(, but I can't, hate, injured, shot dead, wtf","not_for":"Wry self-jokes, mild critique of athletes and argumentative replies are neutral."}}}
